Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 09:36:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 090/154] fix(sidebar): a press outside the sidebar closes its
 open menu
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sidebar document only sees presses inside itself, so a left click on the
page, the floating bar or native chrome left a row menu standing. A local
mouse-down monitor now asks each window whether the press fell outside its
sidebar while a menu was up, and pushes a dismiss when it did. The event is
returned unchanged, so the click still lands.

Leaving the app dismisses every menu, since nothing here will be clicked
while it is away. The menus report open and closed over chrome.send, which
keeps an ordinary click off the script path entirely, and the geometry that
decides the question lives in atrium_menu_dismiss_decision so it can be
asserted without a browser.

The page-side listener moved from the sidebar root to the document: the
navigation row is root's sibling, inside the rect the native monitor excludes.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index ea3030e59ec00..2fe938c707ecf 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -641,6 +641,7 @@ static_library("ui") {
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:memory_saver",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:move_target_decision",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:nav_carve_decision",
+    "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:menu_dismiss_decision",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:native_hotkey_defaults",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:command_bar_actions",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:command_bar_matches",
